  "text": " Them, We measure, we log, we measure, we log, and then we compare the numbers. If the numbers disagree by more than a degree, one sensor is wrong. Next comes the wind gauge, which is just a spinning cup on a short pole. Every turn of the cup closes a switch and the board counts the turns. More turns per minute means more wind, and we turn that into meters per second. Keep the pole away from the chimney, because warm air from the chimney spoils the readings.",
